---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FlipHero from '../components/FlipHero.astro';
import { profile, awards } from '../data/credits';
---
<Layout
  title="Gary Lucy Biography | British Actor — Official Website"
  description="Official Gary Lucy biography: the award-winning British actor's three decades across Hollyoaks, Footballers' Wives, The Bill, EastEnders and stage."
  path="/about"
>
  <article class="rs-page">
    <FlipHero
      id="about"
      imageFront="/hero/gary-lucy-actor-full-length-black-white.jpg"
      imageBack="/hero/gary-lucy-actor-close-up-black-white.jpg"
      altFront="Gary Lucy, British actor, standing portrait"
      altBack="Gary Lucy, close portrait"
      kicker="Biography"
      headline="Three Decades Across<br />British Screen &amp; Stage"
      dek="From Grange Hill to primetime crime drama &mdash; nearly thirty years of British television and theatre work."
      backKicker="The Full Story"
      backHeadline="Read On &raquo;"
    />

    <div class="rs-body">
      <nav class="rs-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
        <span aria-current="page">About</span>
      </nav>

      <div class="rs-byline"><span>Official biography</span><span>Updated 2026</span></div>

      <p class="rs-lede">{profile.bioShort}</p>

      <p>
        Lucy began his career with early television work in <em>Grange Hill</em> and
        <em>Dream Team</em> before landing the role that made his name: Luke Morgan
        in Channel 4's <em>Hollyoaks</em>, a performance that won him Best Newcomer
        at the 2000 British Soap Awards. He went on to major roles in
        <em>Footballers' Wives</em>, <em>The Bill</em> and <em>EastEnders</em>,
        building one of the most recognisable careers in British popular drama.
      </p>

      <p>
        On stage, Lucy played Gaz in the UK touring production of
        <em>The Full Monty</em>. Recent screen work includes Jason Agnew in
        Channel 5's <em>The Good Ship Murder</em> and Michael Curtis in series
        four of <em>The Chelsea Detective</em>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Independent professional coverage includes
        <a href="https://www.itv.com/thismorning/articles/gary-lucy-the-full-monty" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ITV&rsquo;s interview about <em>The Full Monty</em></a>,
        <a href="https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/drama/good-ship-murder-cast-channel-5/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Radio Times&rsquo; cast profile for <em>The Good Ship Murder</em></a>
        and the
        <a href="https://www.tvguide.co.uk/articles/the-good-ship-murder-series-3-episode-1-guest-cast/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TV Guide UK feature on Gary&rsquo;s role as Jason Agnew</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Professional casting profile:
        <a href="https://app.spotlight.com/2933-0161-4591" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">Gary Lucy on Spotlight</a>.
        Current official photography and verified social updates are available through the
        <a href="/gallery/">gallery</a> and
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/gary.lucy/" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">@gary.lucy on Instagram</a>.
      </p>

      <hr class="rs-divider" />

      <h2 class="rs-section-title">Recognition</h2>
      <ul class="rs-rows">
        {awards.map((a) => (
          <li>
            <span class="rs-row-name">{a.category}</span>
            <span class="rs-row-meta">{a.name} &middot; {a.year} &middot; {a.result}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
